OpenLiteSpeed 1.9.3 — the runtime directory comes from LSWS_TMP_DIR.

Upstream compiles DEFAULT_TMP_DIR="/tmp/lshttpd" and PID_FILE in. Everything
the server keeps at runtime lands there: the pid file, the graceful-restart pid,
swap, the .rtreport/.status links, the cgid socket, per-vhost lsapi sockets, the
config-test log, core backups — and the system shm fallback is /tmp/ols/shm.
rexenv runs one OpenLiteSpeed per site, as the user, so two sites on one machine
would share one pid file (the second refuses to start: "already running") and
one cgid socket. And nothing of rexenv's may live outside its app-data root.

With LSWS_TMP_DIR=/abs/path set:
  - every DEFAULT_TMP_DIR use resolves under it (src/util/tmpdir.cpp);
  - the default pid file is $LSWS_TMP_DIR/lshttpd.pid (OLS_PID_FILE still wins);
  - the shm fallback is $LSWS_TMP_DIR/shm/ instead of /tmp/ols/shm/.
Unset, behaviour is upstream's except GRACEFUL_PID_FILE, which upstream spelled
"/tmp/lshttpdgraceful.pid" (a missing slash; dist/bin/lswsctrl reads
/tmp/lshttpd/graceful.pid) and is now "<dir>/graceful.pid".

DEFAULT_TMP_DIR became a function call deliberately: any site that string-
concatenates it stops compiling, so the compiler — not a grep — proves every use
was converted. src/modules/modreqparser keeps a literal "/tmp/lshttpd/"; it is
not built (MOD_REQPARSER is OFF upstream and here).

